String s = "uiiooiiu";
int i = 0, j = s.length() - 1;
while (i < j) { if (s.charAt(i) != s.charAt(j)) return false; i++; j--; }
return true;

Decide which option is correct. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {2, 5, 9, 12, 15, 16, 17, 20};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 25) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 25) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

A problem for careful thought: What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(25);
Node b = new Node(30);
Node c = new Node(10);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Consider the following question. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {4, 5, 7, 8, 12, 13, 16, 21, 26, 29};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 4) return mid; if (a[mid] < 4) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return -1;

